"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.6.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19044) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 27.20.100.9664) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1165G7 @ 2.80GHz (8 threads) - 39.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen opening sub-inspectors (or when performing any other action which does something similar), the focus is yanked to an anonymous, unnamed UI node that, I suspect, does not exist. For example, if I instantiate an `AudioStreamPlayer3D`, go to the inspector -> Stream, assign an `AudioStreamPlaybackPolyphonic`, and hit edit, my focus is forced into a grouping called `@EditorNode@18065   grouping`. I can no longer navigate the UI at all and must force my focus using NVDA's object navigation feature to click a button that is disabled (such as \"Stop the currently running project\") to be able to actually do anything in the editor anymore. I'm 99 percent sure this is triggerable with anything else that does similar behavior to a sub-inspector.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nWhile NVDA is active:\n\n1. Create a new project, or open an existing one, and if needed, set up the scene as you usually would.\n2. Add an `AudioStreamPlayer3D` or similar node which allows you to assign a stream or resource to it.\n3. In the inspector, assign a non-imported resource (e.g., `AudioStreamPolyphonic`).\n4. Click the Edit button, then Edit in the menu that appears. Your focus will get stuck and you will not be able to get out of it.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117245/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117245/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}